description:
lib.rs:306 inside MockBackend::add_notification begins with:

```rust
pub fn add_notification(&self, account_id: &str, notif_id: &str) {
    use jmap_sharing_types::ShareNotification;
    // ...
}
```

ShareNotification is already imported at the test_support module level at lib.rs:247:

```rust
use jmap_sharing_types::{Principal, ShareNotification};
```

The inner use statement is pure redundancy — both names refer to the same item. Remove the inner use at lib.rs:306; the function-body `let notif: ShareNotification = ...` still resolves via the module-level import.

This is borderline bikeshed (no engineering impact, won't fire as a clippy warning on default settings), but it's clean-cut redundancy that would be caught by code review elsewhere. Priority kept at P4 accordingly. Filed for completeness; the cleanup is a 1-line delete.
